.TH "LVM_IMPORT_VDO" "8" "LVM TOOLS #VERSION#" "Red Hat, Inc." \" -*- nroff -*-
.
.SH NAME
.
lvm_import_vdo \(em Utility to import VDO volumes into a new volume group
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.
.B lvm_import_vdo
.RI [ options ]
.I device
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.
The lvm_import_vdo utility imports VDO volumes created and managed by the
.BR vdo (8)
manager into a VDO LV managed by
.BR lvm2 (8).
This is done by moving the VDO superblock by 2 MiB
and creating LVM2 metadata at the front of the device.
The operation is not reversible;
therefore, after conversion to LVM2, access to VDO data is only possible with
.BR lvm2 (8)
commands, and the
.BR vdo (8)
manager no longer controls such a volume.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.
.TP
.BR -f | --force
Bypass some sanity checks.
.
.TP
.BR -h | --help
Display the help text.
.
.TP
.BR -n | --name
Specifies the name of the converted VDO LV. When the name is not specified,
a name is selected automatically. If the converted VDO volume is already
using an LV as a backend device, the name of that LV is used for the VDO LV.
In this case, the name of the volume group must also stay the same.
The automatic name may change between releases and currently selects
"vdolv" as the LV name, and the VG name is selected from the sequence
"vdovg", "vdovg1", \&...
.
.TP
.BR -v | --verbose
Be more verbose.
.
.TP
.BR -y | --yes
Answer "yes" at any prompts.
.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print a shell-escaped preview of commands without running storage-changing commands.
.
.TP
.B --no-snapshot
With this option, the conversion tool will not use a snapshot (COW storage)
for conversion in your $TMPDIR filesystem and will directly manipulate
the VDO device in-place.
Warning: using a snapshot makes the whole conversion transactional and
the snapshot can simply be merged once the conversion
has completed successfully. If an error occurs, the snapshot is just removed.
Without a snapshot, there is a higher risk of problems
with recoverability in case some unexpected error occurs.
.
.TP
.B --vdo-config
Specifies the configuration file for the vdo manager.
.
.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.
On successful completion, the status code is 0.
A status code of 1 is used for failure.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.
Convert VDO volume created by vdo manager into logical volume LV1
within volume group VG1.
.P
#
.B lvm_import_vdo --name VG1/LV1 /dev/mapper/vdo-volume
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
The temporary directory name for mount points. Defaults to "\fI/tmp\fP".
.
.TP
.B DM_DEV_DIR
The device directory name.
Defaults to "\fI/dev\fP" and must be an absolute path.
.
.TP
.B DM_UUID_PREFIX
Specify a UUID prefix for the snapshot volume used during VDO conversion.
.
.TP
.B LVM_BINARY
Overrides the command used to run lvm. Defaults to "\fIlvm\fP".
.
.TP
.B VDO_BINARY
Overrides the command used to run vdo. Defaults to "\fIvdo\fP".
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.
.nh
.na
.BR lvm (8),
.BR lvm.conf (5),
.P
.BR vdo (8)
